    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0356" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/607</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-13T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1919, 8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please note and transmit to Stevens:</p>
                <p>Department is gratified to know that you feel willing to undertake modified plan
                    which has resulted from the negotiations at <pb facs="0357" n="307"
                        xml:id="pg307"/> Tokyo. It is believed that Mr. Morris has shown very great tact and ability in reaching a frank
                    and friendly understanding with the Japanese Government and it is very much
                    hoped that you may now have an opportunity to reap some reward from your own
                    long and patient effort, also the men of the service corps.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
